{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/9sdtps","slideIndex":3,"text":"[3] https://github.com/aaryanadiger/VajraSetu/tree/57d48d1238d04b483a492bf38bbc212b745c98f2. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md and src/services/imageProcessing.ts. Scope shown: deterministic scan path and local result persistence. Captured RGB is normalised using the neutral reference and converted to Lab, then CIEDE2000 difference supports validity and colour decisions. The production build requires native OpenCV support. No image upload or remote identity system is part of this scan path. Optional translation fallback for unbundled strings is outside the diagram. CSV text generation exists, but a secure share/save workflow and remote synchronisation are not implemented.\n[4] https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/ Accessed 26 October 2026.\nEditable architecture diagram corresponding to this Mermaid source (line breaks expanded for presentation):\nflowchart LR\n  B[\"Passive indicator card\"] --> C[\"Expo Camera / 3 frames\"]\n  C --> P[\"OpenCV / CIELAB + DE00\"]\n  P --> R[\"Validity + colour rules\"]\n  R --> U[\"Result + safety text\"]\n  U --> D[(\"SQLite / local history\")]\n"}
