{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/k92pxn","slideIndex":4,"text":"[3] https://github.com/aaryanadiger/VajraSetu/tree/57d48d1238d04b483a492bf38bbc212b745c98f2, docs/SCANNER_AND_CALIBRATION.md and calibration/h2s_curve_v2.json. Five supplied controls at 30 ppm are 0, 5, 10, 15 and 30 minutes, corresponding to 0, 2.5, 5, 7.5 and 15 ppm*h. The chart is an arithmetic dose calculation, not a sensor accuracy curve. The photographed intermediate patches are not monotonic, and the 5/15-minute colours substantially overlap. The pipeline pools that region rather than claiming those doses can be distinguished. The maximum measured colour represents a lower bound at or above 15 ppm*h. There are no supplied replicates or cross-interference tests. The FeSO4 validity decision also remains provisional. Scan-quality checks describe imaging consistency, not chemical confidence. The eight-hour reference period is fixed, not a measured actual shift. Do not use app estimates to establish compliance or make emergency decisions.\nEditable decision diagram corresponding to this Mermaid source:\nflowchart LR\n  A[\"Three-frame capture\"] --> Q{\"Image quality passes?\"}\n  Q -- Yes --> V{\"Validity dot passes?\"}\n  Q -- No --> T[\"Retry capture\"]\n  V -- Yes --> R[\"Colour category + record\"]\n  V -- No --> X[\"Replace band\"]\n"}
