{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/zeczro","slideIndex":5,"text":"Proposed validation and pilot pathway, not a completed trial or an operating commitment. Based on current blockers in docs/SCANNER_AND_CALIBRATION.md and docs/OPERATIONS_AND_SAFETY.md. Success criteria must be specified with the EHS/lab partner before collecting data. Measure false-valid results, unreadable scans, colour-category errors, retry rate and worker comprehension separately. No unsupported claims of field accuracy, safety improvement, unit price or regulatory approval are made.\nReferences, accessed 26 October 2026:\n[1] International Labour Organization. Nearly 3 million people die of work-related accidents and diseases. Published 26 November 2023. https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/nearly-3-million-people-die-work-related-accidents-and-diseases This is global all-cause workplace context, not an H2S death estimate.\n[2] CDC/NIOSH. Pocket Guide to Chemical Hazards: Hydrogen sulfide. https://www.cdc.gov/niosh/npg/npgd0337.html\n[3] VajraSetu project repository, revision 57d48d1238d04b483a492bf38bbc212b745c98f2. https://github.com/aaryanadiger/VajraSetu/tree/57d48d1238d04b483a492bf38bbc212b745c98f2 Primary project sources: README.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/SCANNER_AND_CALIBRATION.md, docs/OPERATIONS_AND_SAFETY.md, package.json, calibration/h2s_curve_v2.json. Local snapshot inspected 26 October 2026.\n[4] Expo SDK 57 reference. https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/\nVisual inspiration only: https://www.canva.com/design/DAHVkQadZBA/8sKx2MfSjISZCmg6W30OqA/edit. Custom AI concept images on slides 1 and 3 generated using OpenAI ImageGen on 26 October 2026. All slide copy and diagrams are editable. Mermaid sources are preserved in notes on slides 4 and 5."}